---

### Overview

`custom_gpt` is a lightweight C++ library and Python training framework designed to demonstrate the core components of a generative pre-trained transformer (GPT) architecture built from first principles.

By implementing both the Byte-Pair Encoding (BPE) tokenization system and multi-head self-attention mechanics directly in C++, this project offers low-overhead inference along with Python bindings for flexible model training workflows.

---

### Key Features

- **Custom C++ BPE Tokenizer:** Node-based Byte-Pair Encoding engine (`bpe_node.hpp`, `hash_utils.hpp`) supporting dynamic vocabulary building, fast encoding/decoding, and serialization.
- **Modular Transformer Components:**
  - **Embeddings:** Learnable token embeddings and positional encodings.
  - **Multi-Head Self-Attention:** Multi-head attention mechanism computed via Query ($Q$), Key ($K$), and Value ($V$) projections with causal masking.
  - **Feed-Forward Layers:** Position-wise feed-forward networks with activation functions.
  - **Transformer Blocks:** Residual connection layer normalization around attention and FFN modules.
- **Python Interoperability:** Pybind11 integration (`tokenizer_bindings.cpp`) enabling model training in Python and rapid inference execution in C++.

---

### Architecture & Mathematical Foundations

The core model processes sequence embeddings through stacked transformer decoder blocks:

1. **Scaled Dot-Product Self-Attention:**
   $$\text{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}\right)V$$
   Where $Q$, $K$, and $V$ represent sequence projections computed using learned weight matrices $W_Q$, $W_K$, and $W_V$.

2. **Position-Wise Feed-Forward Network:**
   $$\text{FFN}(x) = \max(0, x W_1 + b_1) W_2 + b_2$$

---

### Quick Start

#### 1. Build C++ Model & Executable

```bash
# Create build directory and run CMake
mkdir -p build && cd build
cmake ..
make -j4

# Run C++ demonstration executable
./custom_gpt
```

#### 2. Python Training Pipeline

```bash
# Train lightweight micro model
python scripts/train_micro_model.py

# Train on English text dataset
python scripts/train_english.py
```

---

### Repository Structure

```text
custom_gpt/
├── CMakeLists.txt                 # CMake build configuration
├── tokenizer_bindings.cpp         # Pybind11 C++/Python tokenizer wrapper
├── include/
│   └── custom_gpt/
│       ├── attention.hpp          # Multi-head attention layer declarations
│       ├── bpe_node.hpp           # BPE tree/node structure definition
│       ├── embedding.hpp          # Token embedding layer header
│       ├── feed_forward.hpp       # Feed-forward network header
│       ├── hash_utils.hpp         # Hashing utilities for BPE vocabulary
│       ├── positional_encoding.hpp# Positional encoding header
│       ├── tokenizer.hpp          # BPE Tokenizer class declaration
│       └── transformer_block.hpp  # Transformer block layer header
├── src/
│   ├── attention.cpp            # Multi-head attention implementation
│   ├── embedding.cpp            # Token embedding matrix implementation
│   ├── feed_forward.cpp         # FFN implementation with activations
│   ├── main.cpp                 # Entry point & inference demo execution
│   ├── positional_encoding.cpp  # Positional encoding implementation
│   ├── tokenizer.cpp            # Custom BPE encoding/decoding engine
│   └── transformer_block.cpp    # Full transformer block assembly
├── scripts/
│   ├── train_micro_model.py     # Lightweight model training script
│   └── train_english.py         # English dataset training script
└── data/
    ├── raw_text.txt             # Raw sample text fixture
    └── test_text.txt            # Test fixture for tokenizer validation
```

